# Surveillance Center. Same shape as the analytics package above: the directory
# itself must be un-ignored before anything inside it can be matched, and the
# nested provider/transport/media/repository folders need the `**` to survive.
!server/services/surveillance/
!server/services/surveillance/**

# Shared Redis connection used by the Surveillance rate limiter AND imported
# by cacheService. It lives OUTSIDE server/services/surveillance/, so the
# surveillance allowlist above does not cover it — and without this line the
# deploy ships a cacheService that imports a file which does not exist, and
# the backend dies at module load. That is exactly what happened once.
!server/services/redisInfrastructure.js
# AI brain rebuild. These are the new understanding/reasoning layer; without an
# explicit un-ignore they are silently dropped from every commit and never deploy.
!server/services/aiUnderstandingService.js
